the highly anticipated release of james  gunn's half sequel half reboot the  suicide squad  has wild audiences and critics alike  earning the movie a 91  certified fresh rating on rotten  tomatoes  guns movie delivers on its promise of  intense r-rated violence and off-kilter  humor another cast that includes  returning dc stewards and a whole host  of new squad members  the 2021 film finds amanda waller  leading two teams of crazy criminals to  take down a nazi era laboratory called  yotenheim which is rumored to be the  home base of a secret experiment known  as project starfish  we're all gonna die i hope so  oh for god's sake following the critical  disaster that was 2016 suicide squad  there seemed to be nowhere to go but up  the original film was highly profitable  but maybe this time they could make a  movie  most people actually liked the good news  for film fans is the suicide squad  appears to have succeeded when it comes  to quality  winning over audiences and critics alike  the bad news is  this one doesn't seem to be making any  money or at least nowhere near as much  money as the 2016 one did  during its first weekend the new movie  made approximately 26.5 million dollars  at the domestic box office falling short  of expectations that predicted it making  at least 30 million dollars  at the start so what's happened  according to box office analysts the  rise in the delta variant of covet 19  is likely the most significant factor in  why the suicide squad fell  short of his projected box office return  while the beginning of the summer saw  many businesses reopening  states relaxing their mask guidelines  and daily life returning to some form of  normalcy  all that has been challenged recently by  media coverage of the contagious covet  19 variants  according to data from uc davis health  as of july 22  2021 almost 80 percent of the  organization's covert patients  had the delta variant while the cdc  reported a higher percentage at the same  time  the rise in the delta variant has caused  the cdc and many businesses to revert to  previous mass and safety guidelines  suggesting that people need to be more  careful about the possible spread of the  virus  through indoor activities this likely  led many to postpone any plans to visit  a movie theater  considering the high rate of  transmission often found in that  environment  while it's unclear exactly how much the  delta variant contributed to the suicide  squad's box office shortcomings  it was clearly an influence one of the  other main reasons for hollywood's lower  box office returns in 2021  has been the shift from theatrical  releases to streaming like every other  recent warner brothers release the  suicide squad was released  simultaneously in theaters  and on hbo max over the last year or so  that streaming platform has given people  who are unable to go to the theater  a chance to catch the latest big  releases from the comfort of their own  home  other companies such as walt disney  studios are also using a mixed  theatrical and digital release system  though it's unclear how this will change  going forward and whether it's  financially sustainable for the studio  themselves  because of this recent trend as well as  the ongoing shift over the past decade  to more streamable content  it's no longer possible to rely on the  box office as the best way to measure  the success of a new release  even streaming figures are a little up  in the air for example the analytics  company samba tv  has suggested that around 2.8 million us  households  watch the suicide squad on hbo max on  opening weekend  but it's difficult to work out or that  might have translated into ticket sales  considering a household can contain  multiple people nonetheless  deadline reports that the movie at least  holds the distinction of having the top  grossing r-rated opening  for a movie in the pandemic era but that  may be a cold comfort when comparing the  receipts to the movie's 185 million  dollar budget  with so many mixed signals it's hard to  argue that the suicide squad is a  bonafide box office flop  even after you consider those low  returns but it doesn't appear to have  been a roaring success either  at the very least the movie's a good one  we can give them a hand for that  and yes that is your hand very good  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies and tv shows are  coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss  a single one  you
 

